[0.000, "o", "H\u001b[1K\u001b[32m\r← \u001b[1manswer \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[2m(+18.5 s)\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[26;95H\u001b[1K\r  cxpeer/bridge.py: 585 lines\u001b[27;95H\u001b[1K\r  cxpeer/doctor.py: 347 lines\u001b[28;95H\u001b[1K\r  cxpeer/client.py: 246 lines\u001b[29;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[32m\r← \u001b[1midle notice \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[2m(+18.6 s)\u001b[m\u000f\r\n  cxpeer/bridge.py: 585 lines cxpeer/doctor.py: 347 lines cxpeer/client.py: 246 lines          \u001b[31;95H\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m✓ ok\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[2m18.7 s\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[32;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[36m\u001b[1m\r\n── step 5 of 6 · Codex reaches out on its own \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m       \u001b[35m\r\n→ \u001b[1mto codex-journey-26dc: \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[35m\"Run `cxpeer send --to claude-journey \"hello from inside the Codex san\u001b[39m\u001b[35;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[35m\rdbox\"` and reply with its exit code.\"\u001b[39m\u001b[2m\r\n  Codex's sandbox blocks sockets, so its cxpeer send goes through a file outbox the bridge poll\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[37;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\rs\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[38;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[32m\r← \u001b[1mfrom Codex, via cxpeer send \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[2m(+7.3 s)\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[39;95H\u001b[1K\r  hello from inside the Codex"]
